     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also above the usual maximum per dose of about 1,000 formulary-style units (850\u20131,000 mg). Overdosing raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg total per day.** This could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, or another standard regimen.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
